# IMPORTANT:
# Set this to your HOST MACHINE's IP address.
# This is required when a Docker container needs to connect to a service running on the host.
#
# DO NOT use:
#   - 127.0.0.1 or localhost (will point to the container itself, not the host)
#   - Public IP (not needed for local setups and may fail due to firewall/NAT)
#
# How to find your IP:
#   Linux:   hostname -I | awk '{print $1}'
#   Mac:     ipconfig getifaddr en0   (or en1 for Wi-Fi)
#   Windows: ipconfig  -> look for "IPv4 Address"
#
# Example:
#   HOST_IP=192.168.1.10
#
# IMPACT OF WRONG VALUE:
#   - Application inside container cannot reach host services
#   - Connection timeouts / "connection refused" errors
#   - Features depending on host APIs, DB, or services will fail
# Default is set to 0.0.0.0 (placeholder) and will not work for host access.
# Update this to your host machine's PRIVATE IP (e.g., 192.168.x.x) before running.
#Deprecated: No longer required, as application server  dynamically generate the URLs (defaultBaseUrl is always set to true).
#HOST_IP=0.0.0.0

# Images (defaults match current package; override to pin or swap tags).
# Airgap: build/push hiee as nitrogen-j25t11-full; import retags to nitrogen-j25t11
# so Compose defaults below keep working (see readme/airgap.md).
# HIEE_IMAGE=hiee/helicalinsight:nitrogen-j25t11
# POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:15.8-alpine3.20
# NGINX_IMAGE=nginx:alpine
# INSTANTBI_IMAGE=python:3.13-slim

# Optional — uncomment only if you need them:
# HTTPS_PORT=443
# INSTALL_CHROME=true
# POSTGRES_USER=hiuser
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=hiuser
# POSTGRES_DB=hiee
